  "body": "## Cercano v0.27.0\n\nSource: existing tag `v0.27.0` at `c91699b079164138bff083206594f49c56dd5509`.\n\n- **macOS arm64:** Developer ID signed and notarized. CI verified the finished archive’s layout, architecture, macOS 12.0 deployment target, signatures, hardened runtime, secure timestamps, permissions and reported version. It also matched both executable code-directory hashes against Apple’s Accepted notarization ticket.\n- **Linux x64 and Windows x64:** unsigned, experimental archives.\n- **Homebrew has not been updated.** No tap update is included in this publication.\n\n### Verification provenance\n\nArtifacts were produced by [run 43655050601, attempt 2](https://github.com/cercano-ai/Cercano/actions/runs/43655050601/attempts/2). The macOS “Verify finished archive” step succeeded using the source-tag verifier, `--version 0.27.0`, the exact archive SHA-256 `18c68ccc69662da6d18b8017a3eba7eaebc67e057065b90bb66deba2838d2aa0`, and `--notarization-evidence` (without skipping notarization).\n\nAccepted submission: `873414ff-cb1f-4d46-832d-8071e1b64aeb`.\nThe macOS CI artifact ZIP digest is `89a85b1902925be5c4fadb67d5088bacc29fb29eb8d248663536cb64ecdc7bf6`.\n\nPublication checked the downloaded artifact ZIPs against GitHub’s artifact API digests and checked the archive/checksum bytes before upload. Notarization is evidenced by CI verification; the raw Apple ticket was not downloaded or compared locally. These are the existing CI-built bytes, not rebuilt artifacts.\n\nDownload the archive for your platform and its matching `.sha256` file.\n"
